CM_ SG_ 1289 FR_AMK_bEnable "Front-right motor enable flag.";
CM_ SG_ 1288 FR_IGBT_temperature "Front-right IGBT temperature in degrees Celsius.";
CM_ SG_ 1287 FR_Inverter_temperature "Front-right inverter temperature in degrees Celsius.";
CM_ SG_ 1286 FR_Motor_temperature "Front-right motor temperature in degrees Celsius.";
CM_ SG_ 1282 FR_ActualTorque "Front-right actual motor torque.";
CM_ SG_ 773 OilPressure_Kpa "Oil pressure signal in kPa.";
CM_ SG_ 773 APS_OpenPct "Accelerator pedal opening percentage.";
CM_ SG_ 773 SteeringWheelAngle "Steering-wheel angle in degrees.";
CM_ BO_ 113 "MLX90640 right-front tire-temperature cells 1..4, standard CAN ID 0x071, DLC=8. R0..R3 map directly to cells 1..4 in payload order, from RF rightmost/outside to RF leftmost/inside. Bytes 0/2/4/6 are unsigned integer degC; bytes 1/3/5/7 are unsigned hundredths 0..99. Full temperature = Integer + Fraction.";
CM_ BO_ 114 "MLX90640 left-front tire-temperature cells 5..8, standard CAN ID 0x072, DLC=8. R0..R3 map directly to cells 5..8 in payload order, from LF rightmost/inside to LF leftmost/outside. Bytes 0/2/4/6 are unsigned integer degC; bytes 1/3/5/7 are unsigned hundredths 0..99. Full temperature = Integer + Fraction.";
CM_ BO_ 115 "MLX90640 left-rear tire-temperature cells 9..12, standard CAN ID 0x073, DLC=8. R0..R3 map directly to cells 9..12 in payload order, from LR leftmost/outside to LR rightmost/inside. Bytes 0/2/4/6 are unsigned integer degC; bytes 1/3/5/7 are unsigned hundredths 0..99. Full temperature = Integer + Fraction.";
CM_ BO_ 116 "MLX90640 right-rear tire-temperature cells 13..16, standard CAN ID 0x074, DLC=8. R0..R3 map directly to cells 13..16 in payload order, from RR leftmost/inside to RR rightmost/outside. Bytes 0/2/4/6 are unsigned integer degC; bytes 1/3/5/7 are unsigned hundredths 0..99. Full temperature = Integer + Fraction.";
CM_ BO_ 769 "Legacy-compatible GPS ground speed, standard CAN ID 0x301, DLC=2, Display->ECU/WirelessGateway, periodic 50 ms. Source is the latest NMEA RMC speed configured at 20 Hz; invalid RMC status or no RMC update for more than 500 ms transmits zero. The DLC remains 2 to avoid breaking the existing ECU receiver; additional GPS data use IDs 0x067 through 0x06A.";
CM_ SG_ 769 GroundSpeed "Bits 0..15, Intel little-endian, unsigned. RMC speed is parsed in knots, converted to 0.01 km/h internally, rounded to 0.1 km/h for CAN, then clamped to 0..300 km/h. Raw value = physical km/h / 0.1.";
CM_ BO_ 103 "GPS position snapshot, standard CAN ID 0x067, DLC=8, Display->WirelessGateway, periodic 50 ms. Latitude and longitude come from the latest valid 20 Hz RMC sentence and are encoded as signed 1e-7 degree integers.";
CM_ BO_ 104 "GPS motion, validity and compact quality snapshot, standard CAN ID 0x068, DLC=8, Display->WirelessGateway, periodic 50 ms. Ground track comes from RMC; dual-antenna heading is the most recent HPR value and its validity bit expires after 1.5 s. HPR is currently configured at 5 Hz. Signal level is the same 0..4 value used by the display bars.";
CM_ BO_ 105 "GPS reception status and persistent odometer snapshot, standard CAN ID 0x069, DLC=8, Display->WirelessGateway, periodic 50 ms. Odometer resolution is 0.1 km. Max/average SNR and tracked-satellite count come from the latest completed GSV window.";
CM_ BO_ 106 "GPS-derived lap timing snapshot, standard CAN ID 0x06A, DLC=8, Display->WirelessGateway, periodic 50 ms. Times use centiseconds. Unsigned lap times saturate at 655.35 s and signed delta saturates at -327.68..327.67 s.";
CM_ SG_ 104 GPS_RMCValid "1 means a valid-status RMC sentence has been received within the 500 ms freshness window; when 0, position/track fields may contain the last received values and GroundSpeed is transmitted as zero.";
CM_ SG_ 104 GPS_HeadingValid "1 means the dual-antenna HPR quality is accepted and the most recent HPR sentence is not older than 1.5 s.";
CM_ SG_ 104 GPS_LapDiagState "The same diagnostic state that drives the display lap indicator: 0=Inactive, 1=WaitArm, 2=Armed, 3=Approaching, 4=GateMiss, 5=ReversePass, 6=Crossed.";
CM_ BO_ 1792 "Steering wheel unified panel packet, standard CAN ID 0x700, DLC=8. Event-driven and sent only when panel data changes.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 RecorderToggle "PB12: 0=Idle, 1=ToggleRecorderCmd. A 250 ms one-shot pulse; Display acts only on the rising edge.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 ErrorClearActive "PB13: 0=Idle, 1=ErrorClear. A 250 ms one-shot pulse; Display acts only on the rising edge.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 DriveMode "Rotary switch S1-S4: 0=S1/S, 1=S2/Q, 2=S3/C, 3=S4/E, 255=Invalid.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 SlipLevel "PA1 ADC potentiometer quantized to eight levels: 0..7.";
CM_ BO_ 1924 "Steering wheel redundant drive-mode packet, standard CAN ID 0x784, DLC=8. Sent together with 0x700 when drive mode changes.";
CM_ SG_ 1924 DriveMode "Rotary switch S1-S4: 0=S1/S, 1=S2/Q, 2=S3/C, 3=S4/E, 255=Invalid.";
CM_ SG_ 784 DriveModeCode "Drive mode request: 48=S, 49=Q, 50=C, 51=E, Display->ECU";
CM_ SG_ 80 IMU_Header "Fixed frame header 0x55.";
CM_ SG_ 80 IMU_SubType "Packet type: 0x50=time, 0x51=acceleration, 0x52=angular velocity, 0x53=angle, 0x54=magnetic field.";
CM_ SG_ 80 IMU_RawData "Payload selected by IMU_SubType; see decoded packets 0x060 through 0x066.";
CM_ SG_ 96 IMU_Time_Year "Year offset from 2000, decoded from packet 0x050 with SubType 0x50.";
CM_ SG_ 97 IMU_AccelX "X-axis acceleration in g, decoded from packet 0x050 with SubType 0x51.";
CM_ SG_ 98 IMU_GyroX "X-axis angular velocity in deg/s, decoded from packet 0x050 with SubType 0x52.";
CM_ SG_ 99 IMU_Angle_Roll "Roll angle in degrees, decoded from packet 0x050 with SubType 0x53 and SubCmd 1.";
CM_ SG_ 100 IMU_Angle_Pitch "Pitch angle in degrees, decoded from packet 0x050 with SubType 0x53 and SubCmd 2.";
CM_ SG_ 101 IMU_Angle_Yaw "Yaw angle in degrees, decoded from packet 0x050 with SubType 0x53 and SubCmd 3.";
CM_ SG_ 102 IMU_MagX "Raw X-axis magnetic-field value, decoded from packet 0x050 with SubType 0x54.";
